"""The sound audit, part 5: the System's voice, the body's moves, the rappel, what a creature sends at you, the
Inscribing Table, dreams (SPEC §66.7).

The System's UI family was one synthesised voice, a struck glass in D major pentatonic (audio_ui.py and the files built
on it): by rule 3 a ding, every time. Its nearest thing in the game is the game's own struck crystal (amethyst), with
the game's own clicks, toasts and level-up for the rest. The body and the rappel were noise and sine thuds; they take
the game's cloth, leather, stone and rope. Where the game already has the very sound (a critical hit, XP arriving, a
spyglass raised, a grindstone scraping an enchantment off), ours now is that sound.
"""
from audit_kit import E, group, row

UI = group("system", "The System's voice", "Cues, the Holo UI, the band, lock-on, binoculars, Faults. It was one synthesised struck glass; now the game's own crystal, clicks and toasts.")
BODY = group("body", "The body, the rope and fights", "Moves on ledges, walls and pipes, the rappel, and what a creature sends at you.")
TABLE = group("table", "The Inscribing Table and dreams", "The burin, the book, each family's note; a trial dream's four sounds.")

GLASS = "ours, synthesised (the System's struck glass, tools/art/specs/audio_ui.py and its family)"


def u(id, module, name, where, why, *picks, g=UI, was=GLASS, scene="alone"):
    return row(id, module, g, name, where, was, why, list(picks), scene=scene)


